================================================================================
TUMAINI - ANONYMOUS PEER SUPPORT & CRISIS SANCTUARY (UGANDA)
================================================================================

Tumaini (Swahili for "Hope") is a privacy-first, clinical-grade emotional support 
and crisis triage web platform built specifically for university students and young 
people across Uganda.

It provides a safe, quiet, and completely anonymous sanctuary for individuals 
carrying academic pressure, tuition deadlines, family friction, grief, heartbreak, 
or late-night anxiety. No accounts, no phone numbers, and no real names required.

Live Deployments:
- Public User Sanctuary: https://tumaini-zeta.vercel.app/
- Staff Counselor Console: https://tumaini-zeta.vercel.app/staff
- GitHub Repository: https://github.com/fmihaf30-ux/tumaini

================================================================================
CORE ARCHITECTURE & DUAL-TERMINAL DESIGN
================================================================================

Tumaini consists of two dedicated interfaces connected via real-time cloud sync:

1. PUBLIC USER SANCTUARY (index.html)
   - Anonymous Pseudonym Generator: Auto-generates calm Ugandan wildlife handles
     (e.g., "Steady Kob 42", "Quiet Crane 18", "Brave Shoebill 95") or custom name.
   - Emergency Severity Triage Tiers:
     * Tier 1: Critical Crisis / Immediate Danger (High priority, toll-free 0800 alerts)
     * Tier 2: Acute Panic / Severe Distress (Breathing anchors and rapid pacing)
     * Tier 3: Elevated / Breaking Point (Overwhelmed, tuition strain, active listening)
     * Tier 4: Normal / Safe Space (Gentle space to process daily emotions)
   - Real Ugandan Campus Confessions: Anonymously share and read real campus
     confessions from Makerere, MUBS, Kyambogo, UCU, MUST, Kikoni, and Banda.
   - Somatic Grounding Drawer: Interactive 4-4-4-4 Box Breathing pacing guide and
     5-4-3-2-1 sensory grounding reset.
   - Instant Safety Quick Exit: Header exit button or "Escape" key redirects instantly
     to Google for user physical safety.
   - Ugandan Emergency Hotlines: Mental Health Uganda toll-free (0800 21 21 21) and
     Butabika National Referral Hospital (0800 211 306).

2. STAFF & COUNSELOR COMMAND TERMINAL (staff.html)
   - Private Access: The staff portal has no visible button on the user sanctuary to
     protect seeker comfort. Counselors access it directly via /staff or through the
     discreet keyboard shortcut "Ctrl + Shift + S".
   - Staff Registration & Operator ID: Counselors register with Full Name, Role,
     and Password to receive a permanent Operator ID (e.g. STF-2891).
   - Shift Duty Engine: Counselors must "Clock In" to begin handling cases. Shift
     timer tracks active duty duration.
   - Dual Desk Navigation:
     * Emergency Triage Desk: Incoming requests are dynamically sorted by Emergency
       Severity Tier (Tier 1 > Tier 2 > Tier 3 > Tier 4) and wait time.
     * Confession Moderation Desk: Counselors review, approve, or reject student
       confessions before they go live on the public board.
   - Clinical Workspace: One-click case claiming, live 1-on-1 chat, clinical
     de-escalation quick snippets, and group support circle invitations.

================================================================================
MULTI-DEVICE REAL-TIME CLOUD SYNCHRONIZATION
================================================================================

Tumaini features a built-in zero-config cloud synchronization engine:
- Server-Sent Events (SSE) & HTTPS pub/sub bridge connecting devices globally.
- Cross-Device Intake Queueing: When a student submits a session from a mobile phone
  anywhere in Uganda, it pops up in the counselor's PC queue within milliseconds.
- Bidirectional Live Chat: Messages stream in real time between phone and PC with
  synthesized dual-harmonic audio alert chimes (via Web Audio API).
- Offline Re-hydration: Automatically recovers active cases and messages from the
  cloud queue cache upon loading or reconnecting.
- Live Cloud Sync Indicator: Real-time visual connection status badge on the duty bar.

================================================================================
LOCAL DEVELOPMENT & RUNNING LOCALLY
================================================================================

Prerequisites: Node.js (v18+)

1. Clone the repository:
   git clone https://github.com/fmihaf30-ux/tumaini.git
   cd tumaini

2. Start the local server:
   node local-server.js

3. Open in your browser:
   - Public Sanctuary: http://localhost:3000/
   - Staff Console: http://localhost:3000/staff

================================================================================
PROJECT STRUCTURE
================================================================================

tumaini/
├── index.html            Public User Sanctuary (self-contained production build)
├── staff.html            Staff Counselor Terminal (self-contained production build)
├── vercel.json           Vercel deployment rewrites and clean routing
├── package.json          Project metadata and scripts
├── local-server.js       Local development HTTP server
├── css/
│   ├── tumaini.css       User sanctuary styling, grids, and mobile responsiveness
│   ├── staff.css         Staff console layout, duty bar, and triage queue
│   └── motion.css        Emil Kowalski spring motion tokens and micro-interactions
├── js/
│   ├── bus.js            Real-time multi-device cloud sync and audio chime engine
│   ├── store.js          Central state repository and triage queue management
│   ├── auth.js           Staff authentication and shift duty session tracker
│   ├── tumaini-user.js   User sanctuary controller, intake form, and chat stream
│   └── tumaini-staff.js  Staff console controller, triage desks, and moderation
├── assets/
│   └── logo.svg          Official Tumaini sanctuary badge mark
└── public/               Public distribution directory mirrors for static hosts

